.TH OYAMA-HRT-CLI 1 "2026-11-01" "Oyama's HRT Tracker 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oyama-hrt-cli \- command-line interface for Oyama's HRT Tracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oyama-hrt-cli
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oyama-hrt-cli
is the command-line companion to
.BR oyama-hrt-app .
It manages the encrypted vault, PostgreSQL cluster, backups, and data
migration without the graphical interface. Every command that reads health
records needs an unlocked vault; the recovery phrase is read from standard
input and is never accepted as a command-line argument.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS General
.TP
.B version [\-\-verbose]
Print the application version. With
.B \-\-verbose
also print the security profile compiled into the binary.
.SS Vault
.TP
.B vault status
Print
.IR uninitialized ,
.IR locked ,
or
.IR unlocked .
.TP
.B vault setup [\-\-phrase-stdin] [\-\-kdf-ops N \-\-kdf-mem BYTES]
Create a new encrypted vault. Interactive setup generates a 24-word BIP39
recovery phrase, prints it once, and asks for three positions. A phrase
supplied with
.B \-\-phrase-stdin
is accepted for provisioning and tests.
.TP
.B vault unlock-check \-\-phrase-stdin
Read the vault phrase from one stdin line and verify that it unlocks the vault.
.TP
.B vault change-phrase \-\-phrase-stdin \-\-new-phrase-stdin
Read the current phrase and then the new phrase from stdin and re-wrap the data
encryption key. Existing records are not re-encrypted.
.SS Database
.TP
.B db setup [\-\-existing|\-\-managed] [\-\-yes] [\-\-force]
Select an existing local PostgreSQL server or create an application-managed
cluster. The selected backend is written to
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/oyama-hrt/config .
.TP
.B db start
Start the application-managed cluster.
.TP
.B db stop
Stop the application-managed cluster.
.TP
.B db cluster-status
Show the configured backend, paths, port, database, and running state.
.TP
.B db ping
Connect to PostgreSQL and print the database, user, and server version.
.TP
.B db init
Create the database if missing, then apply all pending migrations.
.TP
.B db migrate
Apply pending forward-only migrations.
.TP
.B db migrate-vault [\-\-yes] [\-\-phrase-stdin] [\-\-purge-old PATH]
Import a legacy plaintext application-managed cluster into a new encrypted
cluster, verify source and target digests, and promote the new cluster. The old
plaintext directory is retained.
.B \-\-purge-old
deletes that exact directory after a confirmed migration and requires
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B db status
Show migration versions, applied state, and checksum status.
.SS Settings
.TP
.B settings show
Print the settings stored in the vault.
.TP
.B settings set [\-\-weight KG] [\-\-birth-year YEAR] [\-\-calibration off|ekf|ou_kalman|mipd] [\-\-history-mode forward|retrospective] [\-\-pk-params JSON|@FILE] [\-\-pk-params-updated-at MS] [\-\-updated-at MS]
Update settings. The arguments are stored in the encrypted vault.
.SS Doses
.TP
.B doses list \-\-mode transfem|transmasc
List dose events for a mode.
.TP
.B doses add \-\-mode MODE \-\-route ROUTE \-\-ester ESTER \-\-dose-mg N \-\-time-h H [\-\-extras JSON] [\-\-updated-at MS] [\-\-created-at MS] [\-\-id UUID]
Add a dose event.
.TP
.B doses remove \-\-id UUID
Remove a dose event.
.SS Backups
.TP
.B backup export FILE [\-\-plaintext]
Export an encrypted backup to
.IR FILE .
.B \-\-plaintext
writes the upstream-compatible JSON in clear text and prints a warning.
.TP
.B backup preview FILE [\-\-backup-phrase-stdin]
Preview a backup without importing it.
.TP
.B backup import FILE [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-plaintext] [\-\-backup-phrase-stdin]
Import a backup. Encrypted files are detected automatically; a plaintext file
requires
.BR \-\-plaintext .
.B \-\-dry-run
previews without writing.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-socket-dir DIR
Unix socket directory.
.TP
.B \-\-dbname NAME
Database name (default
.IR oyama_hrt ).
.TP
.B \-\-user NAME
Database role (default: current system user).
.TP
.B \-\-port PORT
PostgreSQL port (default 5432).
.TP
.B \-\-migrations DIR
Migration directory.
.TP
.B \-\-data-dir DIR
Managed cluster data directory.
.TP
.B \-\-pg-bin-dir DIR
Directory containing
.BR initdb ,
.BR pg_ctl ,
and
.BR postgres .
.TP
.B \-\-phrase-stdin
Read the vault phrase from one stdin line.
.TP
.B \-\-backup-phrase-stdin
Read a separate backup phrase from one stdin line.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Print usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/oyama-hrt/config
Application configuration and selected backend. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/oyama-hrt/config .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/oyama-hrt/pgdata
Default data directory for an application-managed PostgreSQL cluster.
.SH SECURITY
The CLI disables core dumps and marks itself non-dumpable before handling
vault secrets, to prevent recovery phrase leakage via core files. The phrase is
read from stdin and is never placed in argv, a log, or the clipboard.
.SH SUPPORT
Support is self-service.
.B Do not contact the developer for support.
Read this man page, the documentation in
.I docs/
(start with
.IR docs/README.md
and
.IR docs/SUPPORT.md ),
and the GitHub wiki first; only open a GitHub issue if those do not answer your
question.
.PP
